  "result": "`POST /api/tasks` now rejects bad titles. `npm test` passes (23 of 23) and `npm run typecheck` is clean. The work is committed as `99ff6bc`.\n\n- **Rule:** a title is trimmed, then must be a string of 1 to 500 characters. An empty, whitespace-only, non-string or missing title, or one over 500 characters after trimming, gets `400 {\"error\":{\"code\":\"validation_failed\",\"message\":...}}`. Nothing is stored in that case.\n- **Bad JSON:** a body that isn't valid JSON gets `400 invalid_json`. Both codes match the error format in `architecture.md`.\n- **Code:** the check is a new `parseTitle` in `src/tasks.ts`, and the route in `src/app.ts` calls it.\n- **Tests:** I added a \"title validation on create\" suite to `tests/tasks.test.ts`. It covers each rejection case and titles of exactly 1 and 500 characters, including a 500-character title with surrounding spaces. It also checks that rejected requests don't create tasks.",
